  "title": "Causal emergence (CE 1.0)",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "37cb26a0-0db1-4143-9180-eaaa25f507e5",
      "text": "Causal emergence is the gain in effective information when a system is described at a macro level instead of its micro level. It occurs when the EI of the best macro model exceeds the EI of the micro model.",
